1result.sql has two practical issues:
• The outermost FROM ( ... ) sub‑query lacks a mandatory alias in most SQL engines, so the query may not run.  
• It rounds profit before applying NTILE, so different customers with very close profits could be pushed into the same rounded value and distort the decile split.

2result.sql avoids both problems and therefore is the more reliable, standards‑compliant answer.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```